From: Emmanuel Velez Garcia <velezgarciaemmanuel25@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 16:49:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Validate enchantment table button index

The button index in PacketPlayInEnchantItem comes straight from the client
and is used to index the three element costs array, so any other value
makes the handler throw ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException.

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ContainerEnchantTable.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ContainerEnchantTable.java
index 5c473bef9a9fa2700ac665f17f4af84add29db2e..6d1aefeeeb6cd5d90751aeb7db7099e640b594d7 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ContainerEnchantTable.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/ContainerEnchantTable.java
@@ -194,6 +194,12 @@ public class ContainerEnchantTable extends Container {
     }
 
     public boolean a(EntityHuman entityhuman, int i) {
+        // VoidSoulSpigot start - the button index comes straight from the client and is
+        // used to index a three element array, so anything else must be rejected
+        if (i < 0 || i >= this.costs.length) {
+            return false;
+        }
+        // VoidSoulSpigot end
         ItemStack itemstack = this.enchantSlots.getItem(0);
         ItemStack itemstack1 = this.enchantSlots.getItem(1);
         int j = i + 1;
